# Playtest report — Snake build 1

**Build played:** release `build-1` of `world/producer`, asset `snake-build1.zip`
(sha256 `2df8ec8d5e9a293df6fe4f8816e486a4b604ecfa75ad2c6d23e10fec1c23400c`; game-developer cb21dad + artist bcf60b1).
**How:** unzipped to an empty dir, `python3 -m http.server 8000`, Chromium (Playwright 1.64, headless) at 1280x800,
real keyboard events (`keyboard.press`) in real time, a bot reading `__snake` state only to decide which arrow to press.
I cannot hear or feel it; sound was not judged by ear (no console/asset errors; mp3s load).
Scripts: `tools/play1.py`, `tools/play2.py`. Captures: `evidence/build-1/` (screenshots, `playthrough-run1.webm`, `run1.log`).

## Verdict
Playable start to finish and the rules are right. No console errors in any run. One real problem: on short browser
windows (< ~720 px of height) the score bar scrolls out of view. Everything else is polish.

## What I played
- Run A: title → Enter → 8 foods (len 3→11) → pause/resume → deliberate self-collision → game over (score 8) → Play again by mouse click.
- Run B: Play again → straight into the top wall → game over → restart by Space → quick double-turn.
- Run C: all four walls (top, bottom, left, right), each died on the edge cell, no wrap.

