## Things that hurt, ranked
1. **Score is cut off on short windows (R8 at risk).** Board is a fixed 640 px and the Score/Best bar sits above it. At 1366x768 it fits
   (board 81–721), but at 1024x600 and 800x500 the page is taller than the window and the Score bar is scrolled out of view
   (board top at −3 / −53 px; the browser also scrolls to focus the Play-again/Start button). A laptop window with toolbars
   (~650 px content) is in this range. Arrow keys cannot scroll back, only the wheel can. Repro: set viewport 1024x600, play, die.
   Captures: `10-viewport-1024x600.png`, `10-viewport-800x500.png`, `10-viewport-1366x768.png` (fits). Suggest scaling the board to the viewport height, or putting the HUD inside the board.
2. **Window blur pauses the game** (`window.blur` → Paused). Reasonable, but if you click outside the page you come back to a paused
   game and must press P/Esc; Enter/Space do not resume. Mild. A "Press P to continue" line is shown, so it is discoverable.
3. **Snake corners are not joined** (the producer asked). Yes, I noticed: at every turn the body segments meet as separate rectangles
   with small gaps/steps (see the crop in `06-gameover-self.png`, top-left). It reads as a snake made of tubes. It does not hurt play, because
   direction and length stay clear, but it is the least polished thing on screen. The head sprite is clear, the tail has a pointed end.
4. **Game over dims the board heavily.** The final snake, food and cause of death are barely visible behind the overlay, so you cannot see
   what you hit. Minor; the Final score is very legible.

## Not confusing / worth keeping
Pause screen, Start button focus ring, the Best score persistence, and the red/green palette all read clearly. Nothing felt broken,
no unfair death was seen: every death was caused by my own input.

## Not checked
Audio by ear, touch input, other browsers, runs longer than 11 length (no filled board), page with `file://`.
